    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.5, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"U4\"], \"pins\": [\"U4.10\"], \"nets\": [\"VCC\", \"BS0\"], \"observed\": \"Display controller pin 10 (BS0) appears to join the VCC bus at the top of the display sheet, via the horizontal wire at the VCC symbol near (727, 310) and the short vertical step at x\u2248703. The BS1 and BS2 pins appear to share the GND return near (716, 323-346).\", \"expected\": \"Per the spec, BS0 (pin 10) is tied to GND and BS1 (pin 11) to VCC, with BS2 (pin 12) at GND. That gives BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 for I2C mode. The observed strapping would be 0,0,1.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`BS0` (pin 10) \u2192 GND; `BS1` (pin 11) \u2192 VCC; `BS2` (pin 12) \u2192 GND. That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration\"}, {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"display sheet (page 3): BS0 10 wire rising to the VCC bus at top; BS1 11 and BS2 12 joined to the GND symbol at the right of the pins\"}], \"impact\": \"The SSD1306 would latch a different interface mode at power-up (not I2C), so the OLED would not respond to the MCU's I2C transactions on DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA and the display would be blank.\", \"confidence\": 0.45}, {\"category\": \"short_to_ground\", \"components\": [\"U2\"], \"pins\": [\"U2.62\", \"U2.61\"], \"nets\": [\"NFC_SDA\", \"GND\"], \"observed\": \"A GND symbol is drawn immediately beside the PB8/PB9 pin area of U2 (pins 61/62). The NFC_SDA wire appears to terminate on the same pin area, so pin 62 (PB9) may be tied to GND as well as to the NFC_SDA bus.\", \"expected\": \"PB9 (pin 62) should carry only the NFC_SDA I2C data line to U3.SDA, with no connection to ground. The NFC_SCL and NFC_SDA lines should each be on their own pin.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"page 1: GND label drawn at the PB8/PB9 pin area of U2 (pins 61-62), next to the NFC_SCL and NFC_SDA wires\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`NFC_SDA` net: U2 pin 62 (`PB9`) \u2014 R1 (10 k\u03a9) to VCC \u2014 U3 pin 5 (`SDA`)\"}], \"impact\": \"A hard short of the I2C data line to ground would stop NFC communication, and the GND tie could also hold the bus low and damage the MCU pin.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The display strapping appears to tie BS0 to VCC instead of GND, which would select the wrong SSD1306 interface mode, and the NFC SDA pin area may carry an extra ground connection. Both readings are uncertain at this drawing resolution, so confidence is moderate.\"}",
